SteamARM: STEAMARM_NO_LONG_WAIT_TIMEOUTS=1 makes waits whose timeout is 60-400 s ahead
never expire (NtWaitForSingleObject, NtWaitForMultipleObjects). The native tool sets it
for Minecraft Dungeons II, whose anti-tamper tears the game down when its long waits
time out; under emulation what signals them does not finish in time.

--- a/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c
@@ -603,9 +603,9 @@
 DEFINE_SYSCALL(NtWaitForAlertByThreadId, (const void *address, const LARGE_INTEGER *timeout))
